// Base Lunar (Moon Base): a lap that starts at an Earth Space Launch &
// Deep-Space Observatory Complex in the coastal mountains, crosses an
// interdimensional portal to a lunar colony in Mare Tranquillitatis, and
// returns through a second portal to Earth's high peaks.
//
// 1. Earth Space Center & Observatory Peak (0..1120 m): the start straight
//    runs north on Earth past a Saturn-V space launchpad, an astronomical
//    telescope observatory dome and giant deep-space radio antennas, with
//    the Moon shining in the night sky overhead. After a straightaway jump
//    crest (55 m), the road climbs +31 m up the forested Observatory
//    Mountain (32 m), plunges -31.6 m into the underground Launch Complex
//    Tunnel (800..1020 m), and reaches the first Interdimensional Portal
//    (Earth -> Moon, 1120 m).
// 2. Lunar Colony & Crater Split (1120..2895 m): emerging onto the airless
//    grey regolith of the Moon (where the blue Earth hangs in the sky),
//    riders cross a steel truss bridge over a lunar rille, pass pressurized
//    geodesic biodomes, six-wheeled lunar rovers, and solar arrays, sweep
//    round the Sea of Tranquillity crater, and climb a two-way Crater Split
//    (2340..2690 m) to the second Interdimensional Portal (Moon -> Earth,
//    2895 m).
// 3. High Earth Summit & Western Mountain Roller-Coaster (2895..4600 m):
//    back on Earth at 42.5..45.5 m altitude, the road crosses 45 m over the
//    top of the tunnel, plunges -40 m into a deep forested valley (5.5 m),
//    climbs +30 m back up the Western Coastal Range (35.6 m), launches off a
//    high-altitude straightaway jump (4095 m), and dives -35.6 m back to the
//    finish line.
//
// Where things are, in metres from the finish line:
//
// - the start sector:            Span(4280.0, 310.0)
// - the Launch Complex Tunnel:   Span(800.0, 1020.0)
// - the portal to the Moon:      1120.0
// - the truss bridge:            Span(1470.0, 1590.0)
// - the east straight:           Span(1360.0, 1900.0)
// - the lunar crater turn:       Span(1920.0, 2290.0)
// - the Crater Split:            2340.2 to 2690.3
// - the portal back to Earth:    2895.0
// - the crossing over the
//   tunnel:                      Span(2970.0, 3140.0)
// - the west straight:           Span(3860.0, 4340.0)
//
// Space center & lunar station colours: orbital cyan (0.12, 0.68, 0.96),
// titanium white (0.92, 0.95, 0.98), and warning orange (0.92, 0.36, 0.1).
//
// How a circuit's file is written: see src/circuits/data.rs. Its mountains
// are a function, in src/circuits/moon_base.rs.
(
    name: "Base Lunar",
    name_en: "Moon Base",
    description: "Centro espacial y observatorio en la Tierra con portal a la Luna:\nlanzadera, antenas gigantes, cúpulas de telescopio y base lunar",
    description_en: "Earth space center and observatory with portal to the Moon:\nlaunchpad, giant radio dishes, telescope domes and lunar base",
    ambience: (
        sea: 0.15,
        gulls: 0.0,
        birds: 0.28,
        cicadas: 0.0,
        wind: 0.28,
    ),
    song: (file: "moon_base.mp3", length: 179.6, loudness: -16.5),
    pace: 1.0,
    layout: (
        control_points: [
            // 1. Earth Space Center start straight (north, -Z) & Observatory Peak climb.
            (0.0, 0.0),
